Subject: [PATCH 07696/11362] [outer-loop] ARC winner-recipe re-diagnosis: goal
 wall is UPSTREAM (perception+dynamics), 8/8 games (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5831)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Source-grounded diagnosis of the 8-game 0-discovery sweep: 8 independent analysts
read each public game's source and compared the true win condition against
gemma-4-31B's goal-hypothesis trajectory. Verdict: 8/8 the true goal was NEVER
hypothesized (0 yes, 0 partial). Root cause 5/8 perception (fixated on the
HUD/budget-bar, never represented the player/exit/target entities), 3/8
dynamics-not-learned. 0/8 helped by budget; in bp35/tu93 the budget bar it fills
IS the lose timer.

Refutes the prior "hypothesis coverage + budget" reading: the goal-hypothesis
generator is not the first failure — several true goals are canonical LLM-plausible
goals the model would hypothesize IF perception surfaced the right objects. The
goal verifier (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5830) is correct but cannot help when the answer is
structurally unreachable given broken perception.

Next ARC lever (corrected): HUD/budget-bar vs game-board perceptual disambiguation
+ action-effect dynamics induction (mover detection). Filed as new gap
GAP-ARC-PERCEPTION-HUD-VS-BOARD. Corroborates project_arc_live_agent_learning_gaps
(perception is the binding constraint) at 31B + full winner recipe.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
